        },
        {
          "id": "1c",
          "path": "cmd/foxctl/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 17,
          "lineContent": "if err := cmd.Execute(context.Background()); err != nil {",
          "title": "Execute Cobra root command",
          "description": "Hands control to Cobra which triggers initialization hooks and command routing"
        },
        {
          "id": "1d",
          "path": "cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go",
          "lineNumber": 36,
          "lineContent": "cobra.OnInitialize(initConfig)",
          "title": "Register Cobra initialization callback",
          "description": "Sets up initConfig to run before any command executes"
        },
        {
          "id": "1e",
          "path": "cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go",
          "lineNumber": 38,
          "lineContent": "rootCmd.PersistentPreRunE = func(cmd *cobra.Command, _ []string) error {",
          "title": "Register pre-run hook for all commands",
          "description": "Ensures config and logger are loaded into context before any command runs"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Binary Startup to Command Execution\n├── main() entrypoint \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/main.go:12\n│   ├── config.LoadDotEnv() \u003c-- 1a\n│   │   └── Load .env files (reverse order) \u003c-- 1b\n│   └── cmd.Execute(ctx) \u003c-- 1c\n│       └── Cobra command routing\n│           ├── init() registration \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go:35\n│           │   ├── cobra.OnInitialize(initConfig) \u003c-- 1d\n│           │   └── rootCmd.PersistentPreRunE \u003c-- 1e\n│           └── Command execution\n│               ├── initConfig() runs first \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go:62\n│               │   └── viper + .env setup \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go:63\n│               └── PersistentPreRunE runs second \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go:38\n│                   └── config.Load() + context wiring \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go:47",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe `foxctl` CLI needs to bootstrap itself efficiently while supporting **layered configuration** from multiple sources. The problem: configuration can come from hardcoded defaults, YAML files, environment variables, and `.env` files—all with different precedence rules. Additionally, the CLI must **wire up shared resources** (config, logger) into context before any command runs, enabling downstream code to access them without explicit passing.\n\nThe bootstrap sequence solves this by establishing a **strict initialization order**: load `.env` files first [1a, 1b], then let Cobra trigger viper setup [1d], then materialize the full config and inject it into context [1e] before any command executes.\n\n## Details\n\n### Startup Sequence\n\nThe binary's `main()` function [1a] immediately calls `config.LoadDotEnv()` to populate environment variables from `.env` files in three locations: `~/.foxctl/.env` (global), git root `.env`, and `$PWD/.env` (highest priority) [1b]. This happens **before Cobra initialization** to ensure env vars are available when viper reads them.\n\nNext, `cmd.Execute()` [1c] hands control to Cobra, which triggers two initialization hooks registered in `init()` [1d, 1e]:\n\n1. **`cobra.OnInitialize(initConfig)`** [1d] runs first, setting up viper with the `FOXCTL_` prefix and loading additional `.env` files by walking up to find `.git` directories\n2. **`rootCmd.PersistentPreRunE`** [1e] runs before every command, loading the full configuration and wiring it into context\n\n### Configuration Loading\n\nThe `PersistentPreRunE` hook checks if config is already in context (for testing), then calls `config.Load()` which applies configuration in layers: hardcoded defaults → YAML file (`~/.foxctl/config.yaml`) → environment variable overrides. The materialized config and a newly created logger are then stored in the command's context via `config.WithContext()` and `logging.WithContext()`.\n\n### Why This Order Matters\n\nLoading `.env` files **before** Cobra initialization ensures that environment variables like `FOXCTL_HOME` or `TURSO_DATABASE_URL` are available when viper reads them. The `PersistentPreRunE` hook ensures **every command** gets a fully configured context, enabling lazy initialization of storage backends—they can call `config.MustFromContext()` to retrieve config only when needed, avoiding upfront connection overhead for commands that don't need storage."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "title": "Cobra Initialization Hooks: Viper + .env Loading",
