        },
        {
          "id": "2d",
          "path": "cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go",
          "lineNumber": 79,
          "lineContent": "_ = godotenv.Load(filepath.Join(dir, \".env\"))",
          "title": "Load git root .env file",
          "description": "Walks up directory tree to find .git and loads .env from git root"
        },
        {
          "id": "2e",
          "path": "cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go",
          "lineNumber": 86,
          "lineContent": "_ = godotenv.Load()",
          "title": "Load current directory .env (highest priority)",
          "description": "Loads ./.env which overrides all previous .env files"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Cobra Initialization Hooks: Viper + .env Loading\n├── cobra.OnInitialize(initConfig) registration \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go:36\n│   └── initConfig() callback execution \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go:62\n│       ├── viper.SetEnvPrefix(\"foxctl\") \u003c-- 2a\n│       ├── viper.AutomaticEnv() \u003c-- 2b\n│       ├── Load ~/.foxctl/.env (global) \u003c-- 2c\n│       ├── Walk up to find .git directory \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/root.go:77\n│       │   └── Load {git_root}/.env \u003c-- 2d\n│       └── Load ./.env (highest priority) \u003c-- 2e\n└── Result: Environment variables populated\n    └── Available to config.Load() via viper",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe CLI needs configuration from multiple sources with clear precedence: **hardcoded defaults \u003c YAML config file \u003c environment variables \u003c .env files**. The challenge is that .env files themselves have a hierarchy (global → git-root → current-directory), and these must be loaded **before** the main config system runs, since the config system relies on environment variables being present.\n\nAdditionally, the CLI uses both **godotenv** (for .env files) and **viper** (for YAML + env vars), requiring careful orchestration to ensure the right load order and precedence.\n\n## Details\n\n### Two-Phase Environment Loading\n\nThe system loads .env files in **two separate phases**:\n\n1. **Early phase** [1b]: `config.LoadDotEnv()` runs in `main()` before Cobra executes, loading .env files in reverse priority order so later files override earlier ones\n2. **Cobra phase** [2c, 2d, 2e]: `initConfig()` callback loads .env files again using godotenv directly, this time in the correct priority order\n\nThis duplication exists because Cobra's `OnInitialize` hook [2a] runs after command parsing but before command execution, providing a second opportunity to load environment variables.\n\n### Viper Configuration\n\nThe `initConfig()` callback [2a] configures viper to automatically read `FOXCTL_*` environment variables [2b]. This means any environment variable like `FOXCTL_DATABASE_DRIVER` will be accessible as `database.driver` in the config system, with dots converted to underscores.\n\n### .env File Precedence\n\nThe system loads three .env files in order [2c, 2d, 2e]:\n\n1. **`~/.foxctl/.env`**: Global defaults for all projects\n2. **`{git_root}/.env`**: Project-specific settings (found by walking up directories [2d] until `.git` is found)\n3. **`./.env`**: Current directory overrides (highest priority)\n\nLater files override earlier ones because `godotenv.Load()` does **not** overwrite existing environment variables—it only sets variables that aren't already present. By loading in reverse order, the highest-priority file's values are set first and protected from being overwritten.\n\n### Why Both godotenv and Viper?\n\n- **godotenv**: Loads `.env` files into `os.Environ()`, making them available to all code\n- **viper**: Reads environment variables (including those set by godotenv) and merges them with YAML config and defaults\n\nThis separation allows the config system to have a clean layered architecture where environment variables (from any source) are just another input to the final configuration."
    },
