      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "foxctl run command execution\n├── CLI command handler\n│   └── executeRunCommand() \u003c-- 5a\n│       └── config.MustFromContext() \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/run.go:61\n├── Executor creation\n│   └── runservice.NewExecutor() \u003c-- 5b\n│       └── stores executor with cfg reference \u003c-- internal/runservice/executor.go:36\n├── Job preparation (lazy initialization)\n│   └── PrepareJob() \u003c-- internal/runservice/jobs.go:35\n│       └── ensureJobStore() \u003c-- internal/runservice/jobs.go:14\n│           └── jobs.Open() \u003c-- 5c\n├── Storage layer initialization\n│   └── jobs/store.Open()\n│       └── persist.Open() \u003c-- 5d\n├── Database connection\n│   └── persist/store.Open()\n│       └── sqliteutil.OpenDB() \u003c-- 5e\n│           ├── os.MkdirAll(dir) \u003c-- internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go:26\n│           ├── sql.Open(\"sqlite\", path) \u003c-- internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go:29\n│           ├── PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL \u003c-- internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go:46\n│           └── migrate(ctx, db) \u003c-- internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go:56\n└── Ready for skill execution\n    └── jobStore.ExecutePreparedSkill() \u003c-- internal/runservice/jobs.go:151",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen you run `foxctl run \u003cskill\u003e`, the CLI needs to execute the skill and persist its result as a job. However, **opening database connections is expensive** (~5-10ms overhead), and commands should start fast. The solution: **lazy initialization**. The executor is created immediately with just configuration [5b], but the job store database connection isn't opened until the first moment it's actually needed [5c].\n\nThis pattern appears throughout foxctl: configuration is loaded once and stored in context [5a], then storage backends are opened on-demand only when a command requires them. This keeps fast commands (like `foxctl --help`) instant while allowing data-heavy commands to pay the initialization cost only when necessary.\n\n## Details\n\n**Configuration retrieval**: Commands extract the pre-loaded config from context using `config.MustFromContext()` [5a]. This config was already materialized during the `PersistentPreRunE` hook before the command even started.\n\n**Executor construction**: `runservice.NewExecutor()` [5b] creates an executor that holds the config and skill metadata but **doesn't open any databases yet**. The `jobStore` field starts as `nil` [internal/runservice/executor.go:36].\n\n**Lazy store opening**: When `PrepareJob()` needs to persist a job [internal/runservice/jobs.go:35], it calls `ensureJobStore()` [internal/runservice/jobs.go:14] which checks if the store is already open. Only on first access does it call `jobs.Open()` [5c].\n\n**Storage layer delegation**: `jobs.Open()` [5c] delegates to `persist.Open()` [5d], which handles the actual database connection. This separation allows the jobs package to focus on business logic while the persist layer handles storage details.\n\n**Database initialization**: `sqliteutil.OpenDB()` [5e] performs the full database setup sequence: creates parent directories, opens the SQLite connection, enables WAL journaling for concurrency, and runs schema migrations. This happens **once per command execution**, not once per operation.\n\n**Cleanup**: The executor's `Close()` method ensures the job store is properly closed when the command completes, preventing connection leaks."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "title": "Database Driver Selection: SQLite vs LibSQL vs Turso",
      "description": "Shows how the storage layer selects and configures database drivers based on environment variables",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "6a",
          "path": "internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go",
          "lineNumber": 29,
          "lineContent": "db, err := sql.Open(\"sqlite\", path)",
          "title": "Open SQLite database connection",
          "description": "Uses modernc.org/sqlite driver for pure-Go SQLite"
        },
        {
          "id": "6b",
          "path": "internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go",
          "lineNumber": 46,
          "lineContent": "if _, err := db.ExecContext(ctx, `PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL;`); err != nil {",
          "title": "Enable WAL journaling",
          "description": "Configures Write-Ahead Logging for better concurrency"
        },
        {
          "id": "6c",
          "path": "internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go",
          "lineNumber": 56,
          "lineContent": "if err := migrate(ctx, db); err != nil {",
          "title": "Run database migrations",
          "description": "Applies schema migrations to ensure database is up-to-date"
        },
        {
          "id": "6d",
          "path": "internal/storage/dbdriver/config_loader.go",
          "lineNumber": 46,
          "lineContent": "driver := os.Getenv(driverEnv)",
          "title": "Check for driver override env var",
          "description": "Reads FOXCTL_\u003cDB\u003e_DB_DRIVER to select sqlite/libsql/turso"
        },
        {
          "id": "6e",
          "path": "internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go",
          "lineNumber": 96,
          "lineContent": "switch cfg.Driver {",
          "title": "Route to driver-specific opener",
          "description": "Dispatches to openSQLite, openLibSQL, or openTurso based on config"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Database Storage Layer\n├── SQLite Direct Path\n│   ├── sqliteutil.OpenDB() entry \u003c-- 6a\n│   │   ├── Create parent directories \u003c-- internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go:26\n│   │   ├── sql.Open(\"sqlite\", path) \u003c-- internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go:29\n│   │   ├── Set busy_timeout pragma \u003c-- internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go:34\n│   │   ├── Enable WAL if not already on \u003c-- 6b\n│   │   ├── Enable foreign_keys pragma \u003c-- internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go:51\n│   │   └── Run migrations \u003c-- 6c\n│   └── Returns *sql.DB \u003c-- internal/storage/sqliteutil/sqliteutil.go:61\n│\n└── Driver Abstraction Path\n    ├── ConfigLoader.loadConfig() \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/config_loader.go:42\n    │   ├── Read FOXCTL_*_DB_DRIVER env \u003c-- 6d\n    │   └── Returns Config with driver type\n    │\n    └── dbdriver.OpenDB() \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go:91\n        └── Switch on cfg.Driver \u003c-- 6e\n            ├── case DriverSQLite → openSQLite() \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go:98\n            ├── case DriverLibSQL → openLibSQL() \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go:100\n            └── case DriverTurso → openTurso() \u003c-- internal/storage/dbdriver/driver.go:102",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nfoxctl needs to support **three different database backends**: standard SQLite for simple local storage, libSQL for local-first with vector search capabilities, and Turso for cloud-replicated databases. The challenge is that storage layers (jobs, cache, memory) need to open databases without knowing which backend is configured, and users need to switch backends via **environment variables** without code changes [6d].\n\nThe system solves this with a **two-path architecture**: a direct SQLite path for backwards compatibility [6a], and a driver abstraction layer that routes to the appropriate backend based on configuration [6e].\n\n## Details\n\n### Direct SQLite Path\n\nThe `sqliteutil.OpenDB()` function [6a] provides the traditional path for opening SQLite databases. It handles the complete setup sequence: creating parent directories, opening the connection, configuring **WAL mode** for better concurrency [6b], enabling foreign key constraints, and running schema migrations [6c]. This path is used by most storage backends (jobs, agents, trajectory, etc.) that don't need driver abstraction.\n\n### Driver Abstraction Layer\n\nThe `ConfigLoader` reads environment variables like `FOXCTL_CACHE_DB_DRIVER` [6d] to determine which backend to use. It defaults to SQLite if not specified. The `dbdriver.OpenDB()` function [6e] then dispatches to driver-specific openers: `openSQLite()` for standard SQLite, `openLibSQL()` for local libSQL with optional sync, or `openTurso()` for cloud-replicated databases.\n\n### Configuration Priority\n\nThe system uses a **layered configuration approach**: hardcoded defaults (libsql) → YAML config file → environment variable overrides. This allows users to set `FOXCTL_MEMORY_DB_DRIVER=turso` to switch the memory database to Turso while keeping other databases on SQLite, without editing any config files.\n\n### WAL Mode\n\nSQLite's Write-Ahead Logging [6b] is critical for foxctl because **multiple concurrent processes** (parallel git hooks, daemon + CLI) need to access the same database. WAL allows readers to proceed without blocking writers, preventing the \"database is locked\" errors that would otherwise occur during concurrent skill execution."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "title": "Daemon Pre-Warming: Persistent Service Initialization",
      "description": "Traces daemon startup showing how it pre-loads config and opens shared resources for fast skill execution",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "7a",
          "path": "cmd/foxctl/cmd/daemon.go",
          "lineNumber": 133,
          "lineContent": "cfg, err = config.Load(ctx)",
          "title": "Load config in daemon start",
          "description": "Daemon loads config once at startup instead of per-request"
        },
        {
          "id": "7b",
          "path": "internal/daemon/service.go",
          "lineNumber": 67,
          "lineContent": "pool := sqliteutil.NewPool()",
          "title": "Create shared connection pool",
          "description": "Pre-allocates database connection pool for reuse across requests"
        },
        {
          "id": "7c",
          "path": "internal/daemon/service.go",
          "lineNumber": 68,
          "lineContent": "sqliteutil.SetGlobalPool(pool)",
          "title": "Set global pool for reuse",
          "description": "Makes pool available to all storage backends opened by daemon"
        },
        {
          "id": "7d",
          "path": "internal/daemon/service.go",
          "lineNumber": 100,
          "lineContent": "listener, err := net.Listen(\"unix\", socketPath)",
          "title": "Create Unix socket listener",
          "description": "Opens /tmp/foxctl-{uid}.sock for IPC with CLI clients"
        },
        {
          "id": "7e",
          "path": "internal/daemon/service.go",
          "lineNumber": 120,
          "lineContent": "go s.acceptLoop(ctx)",
          "title": "Start connection accept loop",
          "description": "Begins accepting skill execution requests from CLI clients"
        },
        {
          "id": "7f",
          "path": "internal/daemon/service.go",
          "lineNumber": 495,
          "lineContent": "store, err := cache.Open(ctx, s.cfg.Paths.Cache, cache.Options{",
          "title": "Lazy-open cache store on first use",
          "description": "Opens cache database only when first skill execution needs it"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Daemon Startup \u0026 Pre-Warming Flow\n├── CLI: daemon start command\n│   └── runDaemonStart() \u003c-- cmd/foxctl/cmd/daemon.go:126\n│       └── config.Load(ctx) \u003c-- 7a\n│           └── [returns materialized Config]\n├── Daemon Service Construction\n│   └── daemon.NewService(cfg, opts) \u003c-- internal/daemon/service.go:65\n│       ├── sqliteutil.NewPool() \u003c-- 7b\n│       ├── sqliteutil.SetGlobalPool(pool) \u003c-- 7c\n│       └── NewSkillResolver(cfg) \u003c-- internal/daemon/service.go:74\n├── Service.Run() starts listener \u003c-- internal/daemon/service.go:89\n│   ├── net.Listen(\"unix\", socketPath) \u003c-- 7d\n│   ├── os.Chmod(socketPath, 0o600) \u003c-- internal/daemon/service.go:107\n│   ├── writePIDFile() \u003c-- internal/daemon/service.go:113\n│   └── go acceptLoop(ctx) \u003c-- 7e\n│       └── [loops accepting connections]\n└── First Skill Execution Request\n    └── handleRun() processes request \u003c-- internal/daemon/service.go:326\n        └── getCacheStore() lazy init \u003c-- internal/daemon/service.go:487\n            └── cache.Open(ctx, cfg.Paths.Cache) \u003c-- 7f",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nGit hooks and CLI tools typically have **~300ms cold start overhead** from loading configuration, opening database connections, and initializing resources. For frequently-invoked operations like pre-commit hooks that run dozens of times during development, this latency compounds into a frustrating user experience.\n\nThe daemon system solves this by running foxctl as a **persistent background service** that pre-loads configuration [7a], maintains a shared database connection pool [7b, 7c], and listens on a Unix socket [7d] for skill execution requests. This reduces hook execution time from 300ms to **sub-50ms** by eliminating repeated initialization overhead.\n\n## Details\n\n### Startup Sequence\n\nWhen `foxctl daemon start` runs, it first loads the full configuration once [7a] rather than on every command invocation. The daemon then constructs a `Service` instance that creates a **shared connection pool** [7b] and registers it globally [7c] so all storage backends can reuse connections across requests.\n\nThe service opens a Unix socket at `/tmp/foxctl-{uid}.sock` [7d], sets restrictive permissions for security, writes a PID file for process management, and launches an accept loop [7e] that handles incoming connections concurrently.\n\n### Lazy Resource Initialization\n\nDespite pre-loading configuration, the daemon uses **lazy initialization** for expensive resources. The cache store is only opened [7f] when the first skill execution actually needs it. This balances fast startup with efficient resource usage—the daemon doesn't pay the cost of opening all possible databases until they're actually required.\n\n### Request Handling\n\nWhen a CLI client connects via the socket, `handleRun()` processes the skill execution request using the pre-warmed resources. The shared connection pool means database operations don't incur connection setup overhead, and the already-loaded configuration means no file I/O or parsing delays.\n\nThis architecture enables **concurrent hook execution** without resource contention—multiple git operations can trigger hooks simultaneously, each getting a connection from the pool and executing in parallel."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Maps the initialization sequence from binary startup through configuration loading to lazy storage initialization. The flow begins with .env loading [1b], proceeds through Cobra's initialization hooks [2a, 2b], materializes configuration with layered defaults [3c, 3d], wires context dependencies [4c, 4d], and finally opens storage backends on-demand [5c, 6b].",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph Bootstrap[\"Bootstrap\"]\n        1a[\"1a: main()\"]\n        1b[\"1b: LoadDotEnv()\"]\n        1c[\"1c: Execute()\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph EnvLoading[\"Environment Loading\"]\n        2a[\"2a: SetEnvPrefix\"]\n        2b[\"2b: AutomaticEnv\"]\n        2c[\"2c: Load ~/.foxctl/.env\"]\n        2d[\"2d: Load git root .env\"]\n        2e[\"2e: Load ./.env\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph ConfigSystem[\"Configuration Materialization\"]\n        3a[\"3a: newConfiguredViper()\"]\n        3b[\"3b: applyDefaults()\"]\n        3c[\"3c: SetDefault home\"]\n        3d[\"3d: SetDefault database.driver\"]\n        3e[\"3e: ReadInConfig()\"]\n        3f[\"3f: Unmarshal()\"]\n        3g[\"3g: Apply Turso overrides\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph ContextWiring[\"Context Injection\"]\n        4a[\"4a: Check context\"]\n        4b[\"4b: config.Load()\"]\n        4c[\"4c: logging.New()\"]\n        4d[\"4d: config.WithContext()\"]\n        4e[\"4e: logging.WithContext()\"]\n        4f[\"4f: cmd.SetContext()\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph CLIExecution[\"CLI Command Execution\"]\n        5a[\"5a: config.FromContext()\"]\n        5b[\"5b: NewExecutor()\"]\n        5c[\"5c: ensureJobStore()\"]\n        5d[\"5d: jobs.Open()\"]\n        5e[\"5e: sqliteutil.OpenDB()\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph DriverSelection[\"Database Drivers\"]\n        6a[\"6a: sql.Open sqlite\"]\n        6b[\"6b: PRAGMA journal_mode WAL\"]\n        6c[\"6c: Run migrations\"]\n        6d[\"6d: Check driver env var\"]\n        6e[\"6e: Route to driver opener\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph DaemonSystem[\"Daemon Pre-Warming\"]\n        7a[\"7a: config.Load()\"]\n        7b[\"7b: NewPool()\"]\n        7c[\"7c: SetGlobalPool()\"]\n        7d[\"7d: Listen unix socket\"]\n        7e[\"7e: acceptLoop()\"]\n        7f[\"7f: Lazy-open cache\"]\n    end\n\n    1a --\u003e|first action| 1b\n    1b --\u003e|populates env vars| 2c\n    1b --\u003e|populates env vars| 2d\n    1b --\u003e|populates env vars| 2e\n    1a --\u003e|hands to Cobra| 1c\n    1c --\u003e|triggers hook| 2a\n    2a --\u003e|enables| 2b\n    1c --\u003e|before each command| 4a\n\n    4a --\u003e|loads config| 4b\n    4b --\u003e|creates viper| 3a\n    3a --\u003e|applies| 3b\n    3b --\u003e|sets defaults| 3c\n    3b --\u003e|sets defaults| 3d\n    3a --\u003e|reads YAML| 3e\n    3e --\u003e|converts to struct| 3f\n    3f --\u003e|applies env overrides| 3g\n    4b --\u003e|creates logger| 4c\n    4c --\u003e|injects config| 4d\n    4d --\u003e|injects logger| 4e\n    4e --\u003e|updates context| 4f\n\n    4f --\u003e|available to commands| 5a\n    5a --\u003e|creates executor| 5b\n    5b --\u003e|lazy-opens on use| 5c\n    5c --\u003e|opens database| 5d\n    5d --\u003e|opens SQLite| 6a\n    6a --\u003e|configures| 6b\n    6b --\u003e|runs| 6c\n    5d --\u003e|checks driver| 6d\n    6d --\u003e|selects driver| 6e\n\n    1c --\u003e|alternative path| 7a\n    7a --\u003e|pre-loads config| 7b\n    7b --\u003e|creates pool| 7c\n    7c --\u003e|shares connections| 7f\n    7b --\u003e|listens for requests| 7d\n    7d --\u003e|accepts connections| 7e\n\n    style Bootstrap fill:#a5d8ff\n    style EnvLoading fill:#fcc2d7\n    style ConfigSystem fill:#d0bfff\n    style ContextWiring fill:#b2f2bb\n    style CLIExecution fill:#ffec99\n    style DriverSelection fill:#ffd8a8\n    style DaemonSystem fill:#99e9f2"
